Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 05:18:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] peer review pass 5: fix what the new e2e suite proved;
 close issues 2 and 3

A from-scratch peer review of every claim in the repository, driven by
a new sha256-pinned end-to-end experiment (six real artefacts: musl
bash/coreutils/curl from pkgforge/bin and the gtk3-demo, Qt6+dbus-demo
and sdl2-demo AppImages from Anylinux-AppImages), all traced live on
the ptrace-denied development host via the seccomp backend.

* src/strace.c: wire the --backend long option (documented and handled
  but never accepted by the parser); decide the backend before
  upstream's seccomp-bpf self-probe and reject --seccomp-bpf and -p
  explicitly under --backend=seccomp; parse
  --anti-anti-debug[=FEAT[:OFF],...] (traceme/status/wchan/all); any
  -c rejected with --json; keep-alive fault deaths report the
  suppressed exit_group's status instead of re-raising the fault.
* src/senotif.c: resolve tracee dirfds (and cwd) when emulating
  open/openat/faccessat -- the tracer's fd table is not the tracee's;
  answer notifications for unknown pids instead of dropping them (the
  tracee blocked forever); emit exit/signal JSON events on reap and
  keep exit-code parity with the ptrace backend; zero revents before
  poll to kill a stale-EINTR hazard; require an actual notification in
  the backend support probe; defer the exec fd-inheritance scan to the
  tracee's next notification (post-CLOEXEC table).
* src/anti_debug.c: rewrite /proc/<pid>/wchan reads (whole value, no
  digits to preserve); cover preadv/preadv2; walk iovecs with a seam
  window for needles split across boundaries; gate every rewrite by
  the new feature bits.
* src/tracing_ext.[ch]: dirfd/cwd-aware relative path resolution for
  --report-files and --json (19-entry at-syscall table, AT_EMPTY_PATH
  handled); feature-spec parser; keep-alive fault-status helper.
* src/file_report.c: record fds inherited across execve/execveat as
  `inherit` operations; escape hint paths per RFC 8259.
* src/json_out.c: emit table-arity arguments; signal events carry an
  optional note.
* tests-ext/: validate.sh grows T8 (relative-path resolution), T9
  (exec fd inheritance), T10 (keep-alive exit-status cleanliness, json
  arity, signal notes), T11 (wchan rewrite, ptrace-gated); new targets
  relpath_target, oneshot_exit, inherit_target, wchan_target; unit
  stubs for the new helper linkage; sanitizer-instrumented trees
  supported by run-unit-tests.sh.
* experiments/60-e2e.sh + 60-e2e.manifest.sh: six pinned real
  artefacts, 41 assertions, passing live (36 passed / 0 failed /
  3 environment-guarded skips in validate.sh); logs committed.
* doc/strace.1.in, README.md, NEWS, patches/PATCHES.md: brought in
  line with the code; AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md replaced by the new
  docs/AGENTS.md router; review pass documented in
  docs/reviews/REVIEW-5.md.
